WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.596
Voice Chief is in early access. Here is how
we set it up together, from your request to
your first spoken command.

2
00:00:08.396 --> 00:00:18.288
Voice Chief is in early access. Email
founder at ironvisiontools dot com to
request the app. Setup support is included,
so you do not set it up alone.

3
00:00:19.088 --> 00:00:33.392
Voice Chief has a few parts. A microphone
window on your PC, a hotkey, a bridge on
your server, speech to text, your terminal
agent session, and spoken answers. We will
go through them one by one.

4
00:00:34.192 --> 00:00:41.576
We set up the bridge together, on your own
server. It receives your voice from the
microphone and passes the text on to your
terminal agent.

5
00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:51.472
The bridge turns your speech into text.
Speech to text can run on your own server.
And if you prefer, you can type instead of
speaking.

6
00:00:52.272 --> 00:01:01.606
On your Windows PC you add the small
microphone app. We walk you through these
commands together: install the requirements,
copy the config file, then start the app.

7
00:01:02.406 --> 00:01:10.584
The app sits in your Windows tray and shows
a round microphone window. It records your
voice, sends it to the bridge, and plays the
answer back to you.

8
00:01:11.384 --> 00:01:19.419
In the config file you enter your server
address. Together we check that the address
works, so the app can reach your bridge
before you try to talk.

9
00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:28.283
The hotkey is push to talk. Hold right
Control and right Shift while you speak.
When you let go, your voice is sent.

10
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:36.838
Next we bind a channel. A channel is one of
your terminal agent sessions, linked to the
voice app. What you say lands in that
session.

11
00:01:37.638 --> 00:01:44.702
Each agent session can have its own channel.
Your voice goes to the active one, so you
never have to choose a target before you
speak.

12
00:01:45.502 --> 00:01:53.164
Now hold the hotkey and ask a question out
loud. Release the key, and the agent answers
out loud. You can also type instead.

13
00:01:53.964 --> 00:02:01.348
This is the point of Voice Chief. It is not
dictation. The agent answers out loud, so
you can keep working without looking at the
screen.

14
00:02:02.148 --> 00:02:07.716
Done. Need help? Email founder at
ironvisiontools dot com.
